:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI VAR=DFTNETTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DFTNETTYPE'.Default ISDN network type
:DATAI VAR=DFTCNNLST USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DFTCNNLST'.Default ISDN connection list
:DATAI VAR=ALWANYNET USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ALWANYNET'.Allow AnyNet support
:DATAI VAR=NWSDOMAIN USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/NWSDOMAIN'.Network server domain
:DATAI VAR=ALWVRTIP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ALWVRTIP'.Allow APPN virtual support
:DATAI VAR=ALWHPRTWR USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ALWHPRTWR'.Allow HPR transport tower support
:DATAI VAR=VRTAUTODEV USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/VRTAUTODEV'.Autocreate APPC device limit
:DATAI VAR=HPRPTHTMR USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/HPRPTHTMR'.HPR path switch timers
:DATAI VAR=ALWADDCLU USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ALWADDCLU'.Allow add to cluster
:DATAI VAR=MDMCNTRYID USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/MDMCNTRYID'.Modem country or region ID
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPNETA.Display Network Attributes - Help
:P.This display shows the network attributes: the names the system goes
by on the network, how it takes part in APPN and alerts, where network
messages and printed output go, and what remote requests may do.
:P.Page down for the rest. CHGNETA changes them; a new system name takes
effect at the next IPL.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SYSNAME'.Current system name
:P.The current system name shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PNDSYSNAME'.Pending system name
:P.The pending system name shown for what the display is about.
